Find my Sim
Introduction
Welcome to the world of The Sims 3.||The goal in The Sims 3 is to improve your character's attributes, wealth, and relationships while simultaneously satisfying all their needs; hunger, energy, bladder, hygiene, social, and fun, in the most efficient manner possible.
Edit Appearance
When your Sim is at home you can edit their appearance via Edit a Sim mode. To activate this mode, simply touch your Sim directly at any time.
Edit your Sim's appearance at any time via the available options. Change anything from clothing to hair style and color, to suit your Sim's every mood or situation.
Welcome to the world of The Sims 3.||The goal in The Sims 3 is to improve your character's attributes, wealth, and relationships while simultaneously satisfying all their needs; hunger, energy, bladder, hygiene, social, and fun, in the most efficient manner possible.||Camera:||Slide one finger across the screen to pan the camera.||Drag the slider on the right up or down to zoom in and out.||Use the on-screen button to toggle camera orbit mode on or off.||Interaction and Movement:||Tap an object to interact with it.||Tap on a location to have your Sim walk there.||Queued Actions:||You can queue multiple actions for your Sim by selecting them in sequence.||In the upper left corner, the icons represent your queued actions. Tap on an icon to clear a queued action.||Needs:||In the lower left corner, there are needs icons. Green means the need is met. Red means the need requires attention.||To the left of the needs icons is the overall mood meter for your Sim; red meaning bad mood, green meaning good.||Wishes and Goals:||Your Sim will sometimes develop Wishes to fulfill. You can choose to "lock in" a Wish, at which point it comes an Active Goal, or ignore it and it will expire.||In the lower right corner, the icons represent your locked in wishes. Up to four Goals can be locked in at any time.||Autonomous:||Toggle Autonomous on/off from the options menu to select direct control over your Sim's actions or allow it to self-manage and act independently.
Town Map
Welcome to the town map! From here your Sim can go to shops, head to work, or visit other Sims. If you see another Sim about, be sure to strike up a conversation. To return home tap on your house or select the home icon from the status menu.
Cooking Tutorial
Keep the pots cooking, but don't let them boil over!||Touch a pot to select it, then shake the device gently to keep the heat down. If you see a pot turning red it needs cooling. Cook the meal successfully to earn a skill point in cooking.
Fishing Tutorial
Go fishing!||Tilt the device to lure the fish in. Wait for a bite and then jerk the device upward in a short rapid movement to hook the fish. Catch a fish to earn a skill point in fishing.
Repairing Tutorial
Complete the circuit!||Drag broken components into the trash then replace them with new ones of the correct type before the time runs out. Repair the circuit board successfully to earn a skill point in repairing.
Cleaning Tutorial
What a mess!||Rub your finger over the grubby spots to wipe them away before the time runs out. Stubborn stains require vigorous attention.
To catch the big ones, your Sim should have a Fishing Kit! They're on sale at the Hobby Shop.
An item needs repairing! Repair Kits are available at the Hobby Shop.
This needs cleaning up! Your Sim can buy a Cleaning Kit at the Hobby Shop.
Gardening Tips
To start a fruit and vegetable garden, upgrade your house in build mode. Your Sim will need to buy some seeds from the Hobby Shop. Fertilizer is also useful!
Your Sim is hungry. Get it to grab a snack from the fridge before it starves! When the cutlery icon in the needs bar is red it means your Sim needs to eat. If your Sim doesn't eat it will die.
Your Sim is sleepy. It should take a nap or have a sleep before it becomes exhausted. When the bed icon in the needs bar is red it means your Sim needs to rest.
Your Sim is exhausted. Make it sleep soon to avoid passing out.
Your Sim has passed out!
Your Sim needs to pee. Make it use a toilet before it wets itself - never a good look! When the toilet icon in the needs bar is red it means your Sim needs to use the bathroom.
Your Sim is smelly. Get it to take a shower or bath to freshen up! When the shower head icon in the needs bar is red it means your Sim needs to bathe.
Your Sim is bored. Get it to have some fun: reading a book or watching TV is a good option. When the jumping Sim icon in the needs bar is red it means your Sim needs to perform a fun activity.
Car Dealer
Welcome to the Car Dealer. Why rely on taxis when you can buy  your very own set of wheels!
Your Sim can now also buy its own car. Visit the Car Dealer to see what's available. Visit the Sims Store Online for all new additional vehicles.
Create-a-Sim
Welcome to Create A Sim! Spin your Sim by swiping a finger across the screen.
