I hope you slapped him hard. Here's §80 for a job well done.
I'm cooking salmon but I'm fresh out. I hear you can fish, so bring me one and I'll give you a new recipe.
Give salmon
Now that's a lively one. Okay, here's your recipe, it's been my family's secret.
I need an egg for my latest recipe. Bring me one and I'll give you §30.
Give egg
I hope it's fresh. Here's your §30.
Man, I'm starving. I'd love a big hairy steak right now. 
Give steak
That's going to hit the spot. I can taste it already!
Fishing would help me occupy my time. I don't suppose you have a spare fishing kit? 
Give fishing kit
That's a beautiful set of tackle. I'm sure I'll get a lot of use from it.
Gardening is a waste of time. I'll give you §50 for a bell pepper.
Give bell pepper
I suppose that will do. Here's your §50.
So you think you can fish, eh? Show me the best trout you can catch, and I'll give you §200 if I think it's better than what I've caught.
Show trout
Oh... That really is one fine trout. I didn't think you could do it. Here's your §200.
For my cooking practice, I really need a ham. Bring me one and I'll give you §80.
Give ham
That's a nice ham. Here's §80 for your trouble.
Marcel thinks he's such a hotshot in the kitchen. Knock over his trash can and I'll pay you §50.
Mention Marcel's trashcan
Ha! His cooking is fit only for the trash! Here's your §50.
