Camera
Slide one finger across the screen to pan the camera. Drag the slider on the right up or down to zoom in and out. Touch the on-screen button to toggle camera orbit mode. Touch it again to cancel.
Interaction and Movement
Tap an object to interact with it. Tap on a location to have your Sim walk there.
Queued Actions
You can queue multiple actions for your Sim by selecting them in sequence. In the upper left corner, the icons represent your queued actions. Tap on an icon to clear a queued action.
Needs
In the lower left corner, there are needs icons. Green means the need is met. Red means the need requires attention. To the left of the needs icons is the overall mood meter for your Sim; red meaning bad mood, green meaning good.
Toggle Autonomous on/off from the options menu to select direct control over your Sim's actions or allow it to self-manage and act independently.
Wishes and Goals
Your Sim will sometimes develop Wishes to fulfill. You can choose to "lock in" a Wish, at which point it becomes an Active Goal, or ignore it and it will expire. In the lower right corner, the icons represent your locked in wishes. Up to four Goals can be locked in at any time.
Active Goals
Touch the icon in the bottom right corner to view your Active Goals.
Lake
Welcome to the lake! A great place to meet other Sims or do some fishing.
Build Mode
Welcome to the Sims 3 build mode! From here you can customise your house exactly how you want it. Buy and sell furniture, move furniture anywhere you like and buy house upgrades.
Tap on the object you would like to move.
Tap on a glowing square to place the selected object there.
Tap on another piece of furniture to select it or tap the large X icon in the top left corner to exit.
Touch wall or floor surface to select, then slide finger left or right to cycle through available menu options. Highlight new option and touch Select to confirm selection.
Menu
Welcome to the menu screen. Swipe left and right to scroll through your Wishes, Status, Persona, Inventory, Skills, Career and Relationship pages.
Simoleans
You do not have enough Simoleans for that! The current number of Simoleans your Sim has is displayed above the needs icons. You can earn more Simoleans by getting a job at one of the businesses on the town map.
Recipes
You can purchase new recipes at the Corsican Bistro by the beach.
